_1781265009861/sessions/2881719096748425028\",\n        \"state\": \"IN_PROGRESS\",\n        \"userPseudoId\": \"2881719096748425028\",\n        \"turns\": [\n          {\n            \"query\": {\n              \"queryId\": \"2356259327783460923\",\n              \"text\": \"Title: Epigenetic and stromal reversal strategies for MASH-associated liver fibrosis\\n\\nResearch challenge:\\n\\nGenerate novel, testable hypotheses for reversing established liver fibrosis in MASLD/MASH by targeting epigenetic regulators, hepatic stellate cell biology, and stromal–immune interactions. I want mechanistically diverse hypothesis generation with explicit ranking, not a literature review or summary of known pathways. Success means a ranked set of hypotheses—including both novel targets and repurposable compounds—that could realistically be validated in human hepatic organoid systems or other human-relevant liver fibrosis models.\\n\\nFocus areas:\\n\\n\\\\- Chromatin remodeling, histone modification, and DNA methylation programs that drive or maintain stellate cell activation and fibrosis memory\\n\\n\\\\- Hepatic stellate cell deactivation, apoptotic clearance, or reversion to quiescence\\n\\n\\\\- Macrophage–stellate cell–hepatocyte crosstalk in fibrosis persistence and resolution\\n\\n\\\\- FDA-approved or late-stage compounds with epigenetic or anti-fibrotic activity that could be repurposed, including rational combinations\\n\\nPreferences:\\n\\n\\\\- Prioritize human evidence: hepatic organoids, precision-cut liver slices, single-cell and spatial transcriptomics over murine-only findings\\n\\n\\\\- Favor compounds with existing human safety data and acceptable hepatotoxicity profiles\\n\\n\\\\- Exclude approaches requiring permanent genome editing or broad immunosuppression\\n\\n\\\\- Prefer mechanistic novelty over incremental extensions of established targets\\n\\nFor top-ranked hypotheses, suggest concrete experimental validation strategies with key readouts (collagen deposition, ACTA2/α-SMA, COL1A1/COL3A1, hydroxyproline, tissue stiffness, hepatocyte functional markers) and go/no-go decision criteria. Clearly identify ideas that look promising on paper but are likely to fail, and explain why.\",\n              \"parts\": [\n                {\n                  \"text\": \"Title: Epigenetic and stromal reversal strategies for MASH-associated liver fibrosis\\n\\nResearch challenge:\\n\\nGenerate novel, testable hypotheses for reversing established liver fibrosis in MASLD/MASH by targeting epigenetic regulators, hepatic stellate cell biology, and stromal–immune interactions. I want mechanistically diverse hypothesis generation with explicit ranking, not a literature review or summary of known pathways. Success means a ranked set of hypotheses—including both novel targets and repurposable compounds—that could realistically be validated in human hepatic organoid systems or other human-relevant liver fibrosis models.\\n\\nFocus areas:\\n\\n\\\\- Chromatin remodeling, histone modification, and DNA methylation programs that drive or maintain stellate cell activation and fibrosis memory\\n\\n\\\\- Hepatic stellate cell deactivation, apoptotic clearance, or reversion to quiescence\\n\\n\\\\- Macrophage–stellate cell–hepatocyte crosstalk in fibrosis persistence and resolution\\n\\n\\\\- FDA-approved or late-stage compounds with epigenetic or anti-fibrotic activity that could be repurposed, including rational combinations\\n\\nPreferences:\\n\\n\\\\- Prioritize human evidence: hepatic organoids, precision-cut liver slices, single-cell and spatial transcriptomics over murine-only findings\\n\\n\\\\- Favor compounds with existing human safety data and acceptable hepatotoxicity profiles\\n\\n\\\\- Exclude approaches requiring permanent genome editing or broad immunosuppression\\n\\n\\\\- Prefer mechanistic novelty over incremental extensions of established targets\\n\\nFor top-ranked hypotheses, suggest concrete experimental validation strategies with key readouts (collagen deposition, ACTA2/α-SMA, COL1A1/COL3A1, hydroxyproline, tissue stiffness, hepatocyte functional markers) and go/no-go decision criteria. Clearly identify ideas that look promising on paper but are likely to fail, and explain why.\"\n                }\n              ]\n            },\n            \"assistAnswer\": \"collections/default_collection/engines/gemini-enterprise-17812649_1781265009861/sessions/2881719096748425028/assistAnswers/2356259327783462455\",\n            \"turnId\": \"2881719096748425028_2356259327783463354\",\n            \"createdAt\": \"2026-06-12T12:43:09.329828023Z\",\n            \"queryConfig\": {\n              \"google.discoveryengine.googleapis.com.Assistant.model_id\": \"\",\n              \"google.discoveryengine.googleapis.com.Assistant.tools_spec\": \"{\\\"toolRegistry\\\":\\\"default_tool_registry\\\"}\",\n              \"google.discoveryengine.googleapis.com.Assistant.answer_generation_mode\": \"IDEA_FORGE\"\n            },\n            \"assistToken\": \"M8gKCwit_a_RBhDqiZl5EiQ2YTJiNWIxZS0wMDAwLTI5MDgtODg3OS0xNDIyM2JiZDU5ZjI\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"startTime\": \"2026-06-12T12:42:20.674543Z\",\n        \"endTime\": \"2026-06-12T12:42:20.674543Z\",\n        \"displayName\": \"Reversing liver fibrosis in MASLD/MASH\",\n        \"labels\": [\n          \"ideaforge\"\n        ],\n        \"ideaForgeInstance\": \"projects/102364069938/locations/global/collections/default_collection/engines/gemini-enterprise-17812649_1781265009861/sessions/2881719096748425028/ideaForgeInstances/6664689606302866253\",\n        \"expireTime\": \"2026-08-11T12:42:19.931266428Z\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"name\": \"collections/default_collection/engines/gemini-enterprise-17812649_1781265009861/sessions/17017783972756749016\",\n        \"state\": \"IN_PROGRESS\",\n        \"userPseudoId\": \"17017783972756749016\",\n        \"turns\": [\n          {\n            \"query\": {\n              \"queryId\": \"11930677366536827430\",\n              \"text\": \"Generate concepts for a sustainable business model.\",\n              \"parts\": [\n                {\n                  \"text\": \"Generate concepts for a sustainable business model.\"\n                }\n              ]\n            },\n            \"assistAnswer\": \"collections/default_collection/engines/gemini-enterprise-17812649_1781265009861/sessions/17017783972756749016/assistAnswers/11930677366536829082\",\n            \"turnId\": \"17017783972756749016_11930677366536827843\",\n            \"createdAt\": \"2026-06-12T11:52:30.781953237Z\",\n            \"queryConfig\": {\n              \"google.discoveryengine.googleapis.com.Assistant.model_id\": \"\",\n              \"google.discoveryengine.googleapis.com.Assistant.tools_spec\": \"{\\\"toolRegistry\\\":\\\"default_tool_registry\\\"}\",\n              \"google.discoveryengine.googleapis.com.Assistant.answer_generation_mode\": \"IDEA_FORGE\"\n            },\n            \"assistToken\": \"NMwKDAjo5a_RBhCYieTiARIkNmEyYjY0MGUtMDAwMC0yY2ZmLWFmY2ItNTgyNDI5YzYyMTkw\"\n          }\n        ],\n        \"startTime\": \"2026-06-12T11:52:07.934719Z\",\n        \"endTime\": \"2026-06-12T11:52:07.934719Z\",\n        \"displayName\": \"Sustainable business models\",\n        \"labels\": [\n          \"ideaforge\"\n        ],\n        \"ideaForgeInstance\": \"projects/102364069938/locations/global/collections/default_collection/engines/gemini-enterprise-17812649_1781265009861/sessions/17017783972756749016/ideaForgeInstances/7792417683852540073\",\n        \"expireTime\": \"2026-08-11T11:52:07.306768107Z\"\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n}\n"
