ilename\\\\]\\\\[DOUBLE_QUOTE\\\\]. - If no meaningful context can be derived from the filenames, ignore them and use the rest of the conversation to generate the title. \\\\[LESS_THAN\\\\]/instructions\\\\[GREATER_THAN\\\\] \\\\[LESS_THAN\\\\]output_format\\\\[GREATER_THAN\\\\] - The title MUST be a summary of the conversation. - The title MUST be shorter than 30 characters and consist of a small number of words. - Summarize in the same language as the user\\\\[SINGLE_QUOTE\\\\]s message, unless explicitly instructed otherwise. If the user\\\\[SINGLE_QUOTE\\\\]s language contains typos, attempt to identify the intended language and summarize in that language. - Try to put important words at the beginning of the title. DO NOT begin the title with articles or prepositions unless they are actually part of the conversation. - DO NOT encapsulate the title in any data structure. The title MUST be a standalone string. - DO NOT use colons or quotation marks. - DO NOT use words like \\\\[DOUBLE_QUOTE\\\\]title\\\\[DOUBLE_QUOTE\\\\], \\\\[DOUBLE_QUOTE\\\\]chat\\\\[DOUBLE_QUOTE\\\\], \\\\[DOUBLE_QUOTE\\\\]assistant\\\\[DOUBLE_QUOTE\\\\], or \\\\[DOUBLE_QUOTE\\\\]Output title:\\\\[DOUBLE_QUOTE\\\\] unless they are actually part of the conversation. - Examples: Input conversation \\\\[HASH\\\\] 1: User: \\\\[DOUBLE_QUOTE\\\\]Write an email to announce the upcoming Google I/O conference.\\\\[DOUBLE_QUOTE\\\\] Output title: \\\\[DOUBLE_QUOTE\\\\]Google I/O announcement email\\\\[DOUBLE_QUOTE\\\\] Input conversation \\\\[HASH\\\\] 2: User: \\\\[DOUBLE_QUOTE\\\\]Attached file: google_revenue_2024_q1.pdf\\\\[DOUBLE_QUOTE\\\\] User: \\\\[DOUBLE_QUOTE\\\\]What is the total revenue?\\\\[DOUBLE_QUOTE\\\\] Output title: \\\\[DOUBLE_QUOTE\\\\]Google Q1 2024 total revenue\\\\[DOUBLE_QUOTE\\\\] Input conversation \\\\[HASH\\\\] 3: User: \\\\[DOUBLE_QUOTE\\\\]Attached file: 123.txt\\\\[DOUBLE_QUOTE\\\\] User: \\\\[DOUBLE_QUOTE\\\\]Summarize the text file\\\\[DOUBLE_QUOTE\\\\] Output title: \